{
 "lesson": 35,
 "duration": 514.6713125,
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.24,
   "end": 8.2,
   "text": "To lose, in French, related to perishable and also forming part of our F to P shift,"
  },
  {
   "start": 8.2,
   "end": 11.08,
   "text": "we said a fart was a little lost."
  },
  {
   "start": 12.44,
   "end": 13.44,
   "text": "Perdre?"
  },
  {
   "start": 13.44,
   "end": 19.04,
   "text": "Perdre. This is an ARI verb, no, P-E-R-D, ARI, perdre."
  },
  {
   "start": 19.04,
   "end": 24.84,
   "text": "So, if we want to say I lose, we're going to remove our R-E and POTENESSE."
  },
  {
   "start": 24.84,
   "end": 27.31,
   "text": "Je perds?"
  },
  {
   "start": 27.31,
   "end": 28.91,
   "text": "Je perds. Good."
  },
  {
   "start": 29.11,
   "end": 33.51,
   "text": "Now, we don't have an E on the end there, making us hear the consonants anymore, like in"
  },
  {
   "start": 33.51,
   "end": 35.11,
   "text": "to lose, perdre."
  },
  {
   "start": 35.11,
   "end": 41.51,
   "text": "I lose, je perds, P-E-R and then DS, which is silent, je perds."
  },
  {
   "start": 41.51,
   "end": 46.38,
   "text": "I never lose. I never lose."
  },
  {
   "start": 46.38,
   "end": 51.98,
   "text": "Je ne perds jamais. Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.98,
   "end": 55.78,
   "text": "Je ne perds jamais. I never lose anything."
  },
  {
   "start": 56.98,
   "end": 59.78,
   "text": "Je ne perds jamais, rien."
  },
  {
   "start": 59.98,
   "end": 62.98,
   "text": "Je ne perds jamais, rien."
  },
  {
   "start": 62.98,
   "end": 64.98,
   "text": "You lose?"
  },
  {
   "start": 65.98,
   "end": 66.98,
   "text": "Tu perds."
  },
  {
   "start": 66.98,
   "end": 67.98,
   "text": "Tu perds."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.98,
   "end": 75.98,
   "text": "Everyone was, tu le mondes, literally all the world, and we know that on time is à temps."
  },
  {
   "start": 75.98,
   "end": 78.98,
   "text": "Temps is masculine, by the way, le temps."
  },
  {
   "start": 78.98,
   "end": 83.36,
   "text": "So how might all the time be?"
  },
  {
   "start": 83.36,
   "end": 84.36,
   "text": "Tout le temps?"
  },
  {
   "start": 84.36,
   "end": 85.36,
   "text": "Tout le temps?"
  },
  {
   "start": 85.36,
   "end": 88.36,
   "text": "Oh, tout le temps. We could also have a contraction there."
  },
  {
   "start": 88.36,
   "end": 89.36,
   "text": "Tout le temps."
  },
  {
   "start": 89.36,
   "end": 90.36,
   "text": "Tout le temps."
  },
  {
   "start": 90.56,
   "end": 94.56,
   "text": "You lose them all the time, you lose them all the time."
  },
  {
   "start": 94.56,
   "end": 98.97,
   "text": "Tu les perds, tu les temps."
  },
  {
   "start": 98.97,
   "end": 101.97,
   "text": "Tu les perds, tout le temps."
  },
  {
   "start": 101.97,
   "end": 102.97,
   "text": "Tout le temps."
  },
  {
   "start": 102.97,
   "end": 110.97,
   "text": "So we've seen how, with our reverbs, we remove our ending and an S for both I, je and you."
  },
  {
   "start": 110.97,
   "end": 111.97,
   "text": "Tu."
  },
  {
   "start": 111.97,
   "end": 114.97,
   "text": "For he, she and it, we don't add an S."
  },
  {
   "start": 114.97,
   "end": 116.97,
   "text": "We actually have no addition at all."
  },
  {
   "start": 116.97,
   "end": 119.97,
   "text": "We just remove our E ending."
  },
  {
   "start": 120.17,
   "end": 122.17,
   "text": "So how would that sound?"
  },
  {
   "start": 122.17,
   "end": 124.17,
   "text": "He loses, for example."
  },
  {
   "start": 124.17,
   "end": 127.42,
   "text": "Il perd, il perd."
  },
  {
   "start": 127.42,
   "end": 129.42,
   "text": "Would you hear the D?"
  },
  {
   "start": 129.42,
   "end": 130.42,
   "text": "Il perd."
  },
  {
   "start": 130.42,
   "end": 132.42,
   "text": "Good, the D is still on the end, no?"
  },
  {
   "start": 132.42,
   "end": 133.42,
   "text": "Il perd."
  },
  {
   "start": 133.42,
   "end": 135.42,
   "text": "So we have P-E-R-D, and we don't hear that D."
  },
  {
   "start": 135.42,
   "end": 137.42,
   "text": "So it sounds the same as the other forms."
  },
  {
   "start": 137.42,
   "end": 139.42,
   "text": "Il perd, he loses."
  },
  {
   "start": 139.42,
   "end": 141.42,
   "text": "Encore means again."
  },
  {
   "start": 141.42,
   "end": 142.42,
   "text": "Encore."
  },
  {
   "start": 142.42,
   "end": 143.42,
   "text": "Encore."
  },
  {
   "start": 143.42,
   "end": 148.42,
   "text": "Like an encore, no, in English we say like when we ask an artist to repeat the song,"
  },
  {
   "start": 148.42,
   "end": 150.42,
   "text": "for example, we call for an encore."
  },
  {
   "start": 150.62,
   "end": 152.62,
   "text": "We're just calling again in French."
  },
  {
   "start": 152.62,
   "end": 153.62,
   "text": "Encore."
  },
  {
   "start": 153.62,
   "end": 155.62,
   "text": "He's losing again."
  },
  {
   "start": 156.62,
   "end": 158.62,
   "text": "Il perd encore."
  },
  {
   "start": 158.62,
   "end": 160.62,
   "text": "Il perd encore."
  },
  {
   "start": 160.62,
   "end": 164.62,
   "text": "So everybody was to Le Monde or the world."
  },
  {
   "start": 164.62,
   "end": 167.62,
   "text": "So everybody is losing again."
  },
  {
   "start": 168.62,
   "end": 170.62,
   "text": "To Le Monde perd encore."
  },
  {
   "start": 170.62,
   "end": 173.62,
   "text": "To Le Monde perd encore."
  },
  {
   "start": 173.62,
   "end": 179.62,
   "text": "So we see how we have an important difference between how E-R and R-E verbs"
  },
  {
   "start": 179.82,
   "end": 181.82,
   "text": "behave in the present."
  },
  {
   "start": 181.82,
   "end": 184.82,
   "text": "And whilst we have various ways of writing the different versions,"
  },
  {
   "start": 184.82,
   "end": 186.82,
   "text": "we can recap those when reading."
  },
  {
   "start": 186.82,
   "end": 189.82,
   "text": "If we talk about sound, with E-R verbs,"
  },
  {
   "start": 189.82,
   "end": 192.82,
   "text": "we simply pronounce the verb without its ending."
  },
  {
   "start": 192.82,
   "end": 194.82,
   "text": "For I, you, he, she, and it."
  },
  {
   "start": 194.82,
   "end": 195.82,
   "text": "Manger."
  },
  {
   "start": 195.82,
   "end": 196.82,
   "text": "Mange."
  },
  {
   "start": 196.82,
   "end": 197.82,
   "text": "Explore."
  },
  {
   "start": 197.82,
   "end": 198.82,
   "text": "Explore."
  },
  {
   "start": 198.82,
   "end": 200.82,
   "text": "And for R-E verbs,"
  },
  {
   "start": 200.82,
   "end": 204.82,
   "text": "we lose the ending and also the consonant before it,"
  },
  {
   "start": 204.82,
   "end": 205.82,
   "text": "if there is one."
  },
  {
   "start": 206.02,
   "end": 207.02,
   "text": "Rondre."
  },
  {
   "start": 207.02,
   "end": 208.02,
   "text": "Attends."
  },
  {
   "start": 208.02,
   "end": 209.02,
   "text": "Perdre."
  },
  {
   "start": 209.02,
   "end": 210.02,
   "text": "Perdre."
  },
  {
   "start": 210.02,
   "end": 211.02,
   "text": "To sell."
  },
  {
   "start": 211.02,
   "end": 213.02,
   "text": "To sell is ventre."
  },
  {
   "start": 213.02,
   "end": 214.02,
   "text": "Ventre."
  },
  {
   "start": 214.02,
   "end": 215.02,
   "text": "Ventre."
  },
  {
   "start": 215.02,
   "end": 217.02,
   "text": "Like vending machine."
  },
  {
   "start": 217.02,
   "end": 219.02,
   "text": "No, that's a selling machine."
  },
  {
   "start": 219.02,
   "end": 220.02,
   "text": "Or a street vendor."
  },
  {
   "start": 220.02,
   "end": 222.02,
   "text": "That's a street seller."
  },
  {
   "start": 222.02,
   "end": 223.02,
   "text": "Ventre."
  },
  {
   "start": 223.02,
   "end": 224.02,
   "text": "Ventre."
  },
  {
   "start": 224.02,
   "end": 226.02,
   "text": "V-E-N-D-R-E."
  },
  {
   "start": 226.02,
   "end": 227.02,
   "text": "I sell."
  },
  {
   "start": 228.02,
   "end": 229.02,
   "text": "Je vends."
  },
  {
   "start": 229.02,
   "end": 230.02,
   "text": "Je vends."
  },
  {
   "start": 230.02,
   "end": 232.02,
   "text": "You sell."
  },
  {
   "start": 233.02,
   "end": 234.02,
   "text": "Tu vends."
  },
  {
   "start": 234.22,
   "end": 235.22,
   "text": "Tu vends."
  },
  {
   "start": 235.22,
   "end": 236.22,
   "text": "He sells."
  },
  {
   "start": 238.22,
   "end": 239.22,
   "text": "Il vends."
  },
  {
   "start": 239.22,
   "end": 240.22,
   "text": "She sells."
  },
  {
   "start": 240.22,
   "end": 241.22,
   "text": "Elle vends."
  },
  {
   "start": 241.22,
   "end": 242.22,
   "text": "Elle vends."
  },
  {
   "start": 242.22,
   "end": 243.22,
   "text": "So all of those versions,"
  },
  {
   "start": 243.22,
   "end": 246.22,
   "text": "no, we have ventre without the R-E ending"
  },
  {
   "start": 246.22,
   "end": 248.22,
   "text": "and also without the consonant before,"
  },
  {
   "start": 248.22,
   "end": 250.22,
   "text": "as far as sound is concerned."
  },
  {
   "start": 250.22,
   "end": 252.22,
   "text": "Which is unlike the E-R verbs,"
  },
  {
   "start": 252.22,
   "end": 254.22,
   "text": "no, for our E-R verbs,"
  },
  {
   "start": 254.22,
   "end": 256.22,
   "text": "we just lose our E-R ending."
  },
  {
   "start": 256.22,
   "end": 259.22,
   "text": "But this difference between how E-R and R-E verbs behave"
  },
  {
   "start": 259.22,
   "end": 261.22,
   "text": "is only for the I, you,"
  },
  {
   "start": 261.22,
   "end": 263.22,
   "text": "and he, she, ith versions of the verb,"
  },
  {
   "start": 263.22,
   "end": 266.22,
   "text": "or in other words, the singular ones."
  },
  {
   "start": 266.22,
   "end": 268.22,
   "text": "The other versions, the plural ones,"
  },
  {
   "start": 268.22,
   "end": 272.22,
   "text": "behave the same way for both E-R and R-E verbs."
  },
  {
   "start": 272.22,
   "end": 275.22,
   "text": "So for example, what did we do for they?"
  },
  {
   "start": 275.22,
   "end": 278.22,
   "text": "For E-R verbs, what did we add for they?"
  },
  {
   "start": 279.22,
   "end": 280.22,
   "text": "E-N-T."
  },
  {
   "start": 280.22,
   "end": 284.22,
   "text": "E-N-T, no, which was silent on the end of verbs."
  },
  {
   "start": 284.22,
   "end": 287.22,
   "text": "So for both E-R and R-E verbs,"
  },
  {
   "start": 287.22,
   "end": 289.22,
   "text": "we will use E-N-T for they."
  },
  {
   "start": 289.22,
   "end": 291.22,
   "text": "For plural people like they,"
  },
  {
   "start": 291.22,
   "end": 294.22,
   "text": "these two verb types will behave the same."
  },
  {
   "start": 294.22,
   "end": 297.22,
   "text": "So we saw to buy."
  },
  {
   "start": 297.22,
   "end": 299.22,
   "text": "Do you remember how it was to buy?"
  },
  {
   "start": 300.22,
   "end": 301.22,
   "text": "A-S-T."
  },
  {
   "start": 301.22,
   "end": 302.22,
   "text": "A-S-T, A-S-T."
  },
  {
   "start": 302.22,
   "end": 305.22,
   "text": "And this verb changed a little bit"
  },
  {
   "start": 305.22,
   "end": 307.22,
   "text": "when we started to play with it."
  },
  {
   "start": 307.22,
   "end": 308.22,
   "text": "Now for example, we have"
  },
  {
   "start": 308.22,
   "end": 310.22,
   "text": "J-S-T, the E of A-S-T,"
  },
  {
   "start": 310.22,
   "end": 313.22,
   "text": "which can completely disappear in the two form A-S-T."
  },
  {
   "start": 313.22,
   "end": 315.22,
   "text": "No, that becomes bigger and stronger."
  },
  {
   "start": 315.22,
   "end": 317.22,
   "text": "J-S-T, I buy."
  },
  {
   "start": 317.22,
   "end": 319.22,
   "text": "How would they buy me?"
  },
  {
   "start": 319.22,
   "end": 322.59,
   "text": "I-L-A-S-T."
  },
  {
   "start": 322.59,
   "end": 324.59,
   "text": "I-L-S-S-T."
  },
  {
   "start": 324.59,
   "end": 325.59,
   "text": "I-L-S-T, good."
  },
  {
   "start": 325.59,
   "end": 327.59,
   "text": "They buy I-L-S-T or I-L-S-T"
  },
  {
   "start": 327.59,
   "end": 329.59,
   "text": "if we mean just females."
  },
  {
   "start": 329.59,
   "end": 331.59,
   "text": "And to sell again?"
  },
  {
   "start": 332.59,
   "end": 333.59,
   "text": "V-O-N-T."
  },
  {
   "start": 333.59,
   "end": 334.59,
   "text": "And they sell?"
  },
  {
   "start": 336.59,
   "end": 338.59,
   "text": "I-L-V-O-N, I-L-V-O-N-T."
  },
  {
   "start": 338.59,
   "end": 340.59,
   "text": "I-L-V-O-N-T, good."
  },
  {
   "start": 340.59,
   "end": 342.59,
   "text": "So for they, E-R verbs"
  },
  {
   "start": 342.59,
   "end": 344.59,
   "text": "and R-E verbs are doing the same thing."
  },
  {
   "start": 344.59,
   "end": 346.59,
   "text": "We hear the verb without its ending."
  },
  {
   "start": 346.59,
   "end": 348.59,
   "text": "What was to wait?"
  },
  {
   "start": 349.59,
   "end": 351.59,
   "text": "To wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 351.59,
   "end": 352.59,
   "text": "I wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 353.59,
   "end": 355.59,
   "text": "I wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 355.59,
   "end": 357.59,
   "text": "So we have an S there for I"
  },
  {
   "start": 357.59,
   "end": 360.59,
   "text": "and we don't hear the D either that comes before it."
  },
  {
   "start": 360.59,
   "end": 361.59,
   "text": "I wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 361.59,
   "end": 362.59,
   "text": "You wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 363.59,
   "end": 365.59,
   "text": "You wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 365.59,
   "end": 366.59,
   "text": "You wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 366.59,
   "end": 369.87,
   "text": "You never wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 369.87,
   "end": 371.87,
   "text": "You never wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 371.87,
   "end": 373.87,
   "text": "Never."
  },
  {
   "start": 373.87,
   "end": 375.87,
   "text": "You never wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 375.87,
   "end": 377.87,
   "text": "He is waiting for me."
  },
  {
   "start": 377.87,
   "end": 381.18,
   "text": "He is waiting."
  },
  {
   "start": 381.18,
   "end": 382.18,
   "text": "He is waiting."
  },
  {
   "start": 382.18,
   "end": 384.18,
   "text": "So all of these versions know"
  },
  {
   "start": 384.18,
   "end": 386.18,
   "text": "these singular versions"
  },
  {
   "start": 386.18,
   "end": 387.18,
   "text": "I wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 387.18,
   "end": 388.18,
   "text": "You wait."
  },
  {
   "start": 388.18,
   "end": 390.18,
   "text": "He waits."
  },
  {
   "start": 390.18,
   "end": 393.18,
   "text": "Are doing something different to the E-R verbs now"
  },
  {
   "start": 393.18,
   "end": 395.18,
   "text": "but for they, for the plural person"
  },
  {
   "start": 395.18,
   "end": 398.18,
   "text": "R-E verbs behave just like E-R verbs"
  },
  {
   "start": 398.18,
   "end": 400.18,
   "text": "we add E-N-T for they."
  },
  {
   "start": 400.18,
   "end": 402.18,
   "text": "They are waiting for me."
  },
  {
   "start": 402.18,
   "end": 405.53,
   "text": "He is waiting."
  },
  {
   "start": 405.53,
   "end": 406.53,
   "text": "He is waiting."
  },
  {
   "start": 406.53,
   "end": 408.53,
   "text": "So the E-N-T is silent now"
  },
  {
   "start": 408.53,
   "end": 410.53,
   "text": "but it of course makes us hear that D"
  },
  {
   "start": 410.53,
   "end": 412.53,
   "text": "that comes before that E-N-T"
  },
  {
   "start": 412.53,
   "end": 414.53,
   "text": "Il m'attend."
  },
  {
   "start": 414.53,
   "end": 416.53,
   "text": "They are waiting for me."
  },
  {
   "start": 416.53,
   "end": 418.53,
   "text": "But just he is waiting for me."
  },
  {
   "start": 420.53,
   "end": 421.53,
   "text": "Il m'attend."
  },
  {
   "start": 421.53,
   "end": 422.53,
   "text": "Il m'attend."
  },
  {
   "start": 422.53,
   "end": 424.53,
   "text": "Here we don't hear the last D."
  },
  {
   "start": 424.53,
   "end": 425.53,
   "text": "Il m'attend."
  },
  {
   "start": 425.53,
   "end": 427.53,
   "text": "We saw quesque"
  },
  {
   "start": 427.53,
   "end": 429.53,
   "text": "which is one of the ways we can say what"
  },
  {
   "start": 429.53,
   "end": 431.53,
   "text": "literally what is it that"
  },
  {
   "start": 431.53,
   "end": 432.53,
   "text": "how would you say"
  },
  {
   "start": 432.53,
   "end": 434.53,
   "text": "what is it that"
  },
  {
